I was able to patch angular to fix the issue. I created a new `moveNodesAfterSibling` that uses `insertAfter`. Going to try putting this into ng proper and running the suite, but for starters here's my code (es5 transpiled):

``` javascript
  function moveNodesAfterSibling2(sibling, nodes) {
    var cs = sibling;
    if (nodes.length > 0 && lang_1.isPresent(dom_adapter_1.DOM.parentElement(sibling))) {
      for (var i = 0; i < nodes.length; i++) {
        //dom_adapter_1.DOM.insertBefore(sibling, nodes[i]);
        dom_adapter_1.DOM.insertAfter(cs, nodes[i]);
        cs = nodes[i];
      }
      //dom_adapter_1.DOM.insertBefore(nodes[0], sibling);
    }
  }
```
